You should go around Sydney city by taking the Sydney Explorer, a bus which regularly goes round the city. You can ride on that bus as long as you like.
It'd be convenient for us to do some sightseeing in this city using this bus, wouldn't it?
Yes, it would be. Needless to say, you can take a taxi if you are in a hurry. It's completely up to you. You'll find a "VACANCY" sign indicating that the taxi is available, and you'll see an "ENGAGED" sign if the taxi is not available.
First of all, you ought to visit the Sydney Opera House, the symbol of Sydney. During daytime you can see Opera House, uniquely built in the shape of big white sails.
Would it be possible for me to watch an opera or go to a music concert at night?
Yes, it is. Why don't you have lunch at the Sydney Tower, the tallest building in Sydney, from where you can enjoy a panoramic view of the city?
Yes, I'd love to take lunch up there.
Next, take a walk around the Rocks area and visit the Australian Museum. You'll be able to learn a lot about Australia. You can also get nice gifts at Darling Harbor if you want to buy some souvenirs. There are many kinds of goods and articles you might like to purchase.
What are the other sights you suggest?
I suggest you drive out of the city and visit the Featherdale Wildlife Park, well-known for its koalas, and the Blue Mountains, noted for their beautiful deep valleys and steep cliffs. You could also enjoy the Sydney Harbor cruise at night.
There are many other places I want to visit around Australia, such as Canberra, the capital of Australia, Melbourne, the Gold Coast, and Cairns.
There are a lot of sights to visit here, aren't there?
As you know, the United Kingdom is made up of England, Wales, and Scotland. Northern Ireland is also part of it.
