That's true. There are great men who are buried in this abbey, such as Darwin, Newton, Milton and Dickens. The Tower of London is also a "must" on your itinerary if you are interested in historical structures or monuments.
Is a visit to the Tower of London on our itinerary?
No, it isn't. However I suggest you visit it. You can see there the swords of many English kings and the Crown jewels of many English Monarchs. You can also see the Houses of Parliament, which may be easily recognized by their Gothic architecture and the famous Big Ben clock tower.
